Senior Quality Engineer CSV | Salary up to €89,820 per year | Hoofddorp, North Holland | Full-Time, 40h p/week, On-Site Pharmaceutical & Biotechnology Industry

Looking to have your CSV and Quality Oversight skills contribute to improve the lives of cancer patients all over the world? 
This new Senior Quality Engineer CSV position will allow you to do exactly that, as you'll be responsible for supporting Manufacturing Execution System (MES) projects through Quality Oversight and Quality Risk Management oversight activities.

About the Company:
Our client is a biopharmaceutical company located in Hoofddorp, focused on the development and commercialization of novel cancer immunotherapy products, designed to restore the patient's immune system to recognize and eradicate tumors, that are shipped to and from all across Europe. Their state-of-the-art facility includes MP/ML-II cleanrooms, GMP warehouses, quality control lab, PCR lab, offices, learning environments, auditing rooms, a town hall, auditorium and a restaurant.

Offer:
Salary: up to €89,820 per year;
Contract: Initial 12 month contract via Gi Life Sciences with possibility of extension;
Location: Hoofddorp, North Holland;
Work Model: Full-Time, 40h p/week, On-site;
Work Schedule: Monday-Friday, 9:00-17:00;

Key Responsibilities:
Support KPI development to drive improvement initiatives across the organization.
Help implement process changes and review/approve CSV validation and revalidation deliverables.
Ensure compliance with regulatory requirements, GMP, and quality processes.
Maintain quality programs and support complex issue resolution, deviation assessment, and impact evaluation.
Work with cross-functional teams and operating entities to support inspections, SPC analyses, audits, and site quality oversight activities.
Manage priorities independently on routine work and support CQV and Quality Risk Management oversight for the site.

Qualifications and Experience
BSc diploma in relevant area such as Engineering, Computer Science, Information Technology / Information Systems;
Relevant experience in the application of Quality principles, concepts, industry practices, and standards;
Knowledge and experience with Werum PAS-X;
Clear communication, technical writing and good interpersonal skills;
Preferably: Knowledge of Six Sigma, Define-Measure-Analyze-Improve-Control (DMAIC) methodology, or Risk Management tools (eg: HACCP);

Interested?
Apply now by submitting your updated CV, and feel free to contact:
Audrey Poluakan Recruitment Consultant at Gi Life Sciences Netherlands
M: 0658069570
E: audrey.poluakan@gigroup.com
